{"type":"FeatureCollection","_meta":{"title":"Hungary: hate-related crimes registered by police and other investigating authorities, by county, two periods","measures":"Registered crimes (ENyÜBS crime statistics) by county where the crime was committed, for Criminal Code (Btk.) sections 216 \"violence against a member of a community\" (the hate-crime offence), 332 \"incitement against a community\", and 333 \"public denial of the crimes of the National Socialist or communist regimes\"; all_registered_crimes for context. Blank cells in the source mean no registered crime and are written as 0. Keys are periods, not single years: 2013-01_to_2018-06 (2013-01-01 to 2018-06-30) and 2018-07_to_latest (2018-07-01 to the latest month in the source workbook, file version dated 2026-10-06; BSR updates on the 5th working day after each month closes). value = Btk. 216 in the second period.","notes":["The BSR public site shows these as Excel pivot tables with a year slicer; only the default view (all years pooled) could be read automatically. Year-by-year figures need the slicer, by hand, at https://bsr.bm.hu/Document (the site says reports open only in Firefox).","The 2013-2018 workbook notes that data reporting paused July-November 2013 because of a system changeover.","Rows \"Országhatáron kívüli tevékenység\" (activity outside the borders), \"Az ország területre nem bontható adatai\" (not attributable to an area) and \"(üres)\" (blank) are kept without geometry.","The 2018-07 workbook has no grand-total column, so the \"Hungary (all areas)\" figures for that period are the sum of every published area column (including the not-attributable and outside-borders columns).","The full pivot (every offence row x county x period) is in hu_registered_crimes_by_county_all_offences.csv."],"source":"Belügyminisztérium (Ministry of the Interior), Bűnügyi Statisztikai Rendszer (BSR): \"Regisztrált bűncselekmények száma az elkövetés helye szerint 2013.01.01-2018.06.30\" and \"... 2018. II. 